  "answer_text": "**The comic came first!** Here's a quick breakdown:\n\n- **The Comic Book:** *The Walking Dead* is an American post-apocalyptic comic book series created by writer Robert Kirkman and artist Tony Moore. It began publishing in **2003** by Image Comics and ran for 193 issues, with Kirkman unexpectedly ending the series in 2019.\n\n- **The TV Show:** AMC picked up the rights to make a series based on the comic in 2009, ordered a pilot episode on January 21, 2010, and the series premiered on **October 31, 2010**.\n\nSo the comic book predates the TV show by **about 7 years**. The AMC television series *(2010\u20132022)* loosely follows the storyline of the comic book.",
